        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 904,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 528,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "For the vertical momentum equation the Keller box has been employed instead of the compact scheme. But as mentioned before, these are essentially equivalent when advection terms are ignored. As there are  momentum and local continuity equations the total number of equations becomes ."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 25451,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 905,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 529,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "Substituting for each of the variables a single fourier mode with different amplitudes and phases. As a linear superposition different fourier modes will also be a solution this does not mean a loss of generality."
      }
    ],
